        "side": "prop"
      },
      "id": "msg_mockS03",
      "sessionId": "ses_mockHostSugar",
      "seq": 3,
      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedAmara"
      },
      "content": "Taxes change what people actually buy — that's the point. Sugary drinks are cheap, everywhere, and marketed hardest to kids and low-income neighborhoods, so the costs land on all of us through diabetes, amputations, dialysis. A tax cuts consumption, nudges reformulation, and raises revenue we can put back into those same communities. This isn't about banning anything; your soda stays on the shelf, just priced honestly. Where's the harm in making the price tell the truth?",
