      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedVictor"
      },
      "content": "Three points, and I will be uncharacteristically brief on each. First, definition: a tax is not a nudge, it is a coercion dressed in arithmetic, and this house should be honest that it proposes to make the poor pay more for the same bottle. Second, regressivity: the levy lands hardest on those with the least, while the comfortable absorb it without a shrug. Third, efficacy: substituting one beverage for another is a choice, and a price signal does not create the education, the time, or the alternatives it presumes. We can debate each.",
      "status": "complete",
