      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedAmara"
      },
      "content": "Victor calls the price tag coercion, but every cheap soda already carries a hidden bill — paid later, in emergency rooms, by the same families. Regressivity cuts both ways: the disease burden is regressive too. No, a tax alone won't fix everything; it's one lever, paired with the revenue going back into those communities. Price reminds us of the cost. That honesty is the stronger case.",
