      "author": {
        "type": "character",
        "characterId": "chr_seedVictor"
      },
      "content": "Kai, the single question left open is this: when a government raises the price of a lawful good, does it cure the harm or merely relocate the burden? My colleague answers that the disease bill is regressive too, and I grant it. But granting a harm exists is not the same as proving your instrument reaches it; a levy on a bottle taxes the purchase, not the outcome. Define your terms. The motion says tax; it does not say cure. On the record as it stands, the price has been made to speak, and what it says is arithmetic, not health. The house should decline the motion.",
